* @title Recursive pattern inserts leadering for runs of blanks
* @attribution Griswold 1971, Chapter 2, Section 2.16.5
* @input >>>
* INSERT          LEADERING
* TRY TWO BLANKS
* TRY THREE   BLANKS
* TRY FOUR    BLANKS
* TRY FIVE     BLANKS
* TRY    SEVERAL      BREAKS
* FINALLY, TRY
* A RIGHT JUSTIFIED ONE.
* <<<
* @expect >>>
* INSERT          LEADERING
* INSERT . . . . . LEADERING
* TRY TWO BLANKS
* TRY TWO BLANKS
* TRY THREE   BLANKS
* TRY THREE . BLANKS
* TRY FOUR    BLANKS
* TRY FOUR . . BLANKS
* TRY FIVE     BLANKS
* TRY FIVE . . BLANKS
* TRY    SEVERAL      BREAKS
* TRY . . SEVERAL . . . BREAKS
* FINALLY, TRY
* FINALLY, TRY
* A RIGHT JUSTIFIED ONE.
* A RIGHT JUSTIFIED ONE.
* <<<
          &TRIM = 1
          P = ' ' *P | ' '
          PAT = @Y ' ' P @X
LOOP      CARD = INPUT :F(END)
          OUTPUT = CARD
LOOP1     CARD PAT = DUPL(' .',(X - Y) / 2) ' ' :S(LOOP1)
          OUTPUT = CARD :(LOOP)
END
